div.p:
Con:—would first need Soviet commitment publicly
                    to resist efforts to incorporate exceptions into proposal covering terrorist
                    acts by “national liberation groups”;

—would cause grave concern among certain member of Congress and ethnic
                    organizations who would prefer that a person fleeing the U.S.S.R. by hijacking
                    an aircraft be prosecuted in the U.S. rather than returned to the U.S.S.R.;

Pro:—would publicly underline U.S.-Soviet
resolve against certain terrorist acts (scope to be determined in
declaration);

Con:—some states might regard Soviet involvement
as another sign of big-power interference in internal affair and react
adversely;
